Input: {"question": "Who is the artist of the album \"Golden Hits\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d00", "start": 0, "end": 129, "text": "The Drifters' Golden Hits The Drifters' Golden Hits is a 1968 compilation album by American doo wop/R&B vocal group The Drifters."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d00", "start": 130, "end": 259, "text": "The collection of the bands' later hits charted at #22 on Billboard's \"Black Albums\" chart and at #122 on the \"Pop Albums\" chart."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d00", "start": 260, "end": 375, "text": "Music critic Robert Christgau numbers it among the essentials for a basic library of albums representing the 1960s."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d00", "start": 376, "end": 491, "text": "In 2003, \"Rolling Stone\" listed the album at #465 in its list of \"Rolling Stone's 500 Greatest Albums of All Time\"."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d00", "start": 492, "end": 584, "text": "Originally released on the Atlantic label, the album has been re-released on CD by Atlantic."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d00", "start": 585, "end": 596, "text": "A Drifters'"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d01", "start": 0, "end": 382, "text": "golden age of The Drifters , and while changes occurred during that timeframe as well , this was essentially who the historic drifters were , where they graced the world with staggering hits such as “ On Broadway ” , “ There Goes My Baby ” , “ Up On The Roof ” and “ Under The Boardwalk ” a crossover track that was even covered by The Rolling Stones during their early R & B days ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d01", "start": 383, "end": 484, "text": "﻿ While not able to produce a great number of first rate hits , when they did click , their music was"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d02", "start": 0, "end": 164, "text": "Night At The Movies The Beatles More by The Beatles Under the Boardwalk Save the Last Dance for Me The Good Life With the Beatles White Christmas / The Bells of St."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d02", "start": 165, "end": 544, "text": "Mary's Rockin'& Driftin'Clyde McPhatter & The Beatles I 'll Take You Where the Music's Playing The Christmas Song / I Remember Christmas Baby What I Mean : Northern Soul Sides Legacy Of The Beatles ( Live ) © 2019 Revolver Records ℗ 2019 Revolver Records Company About Jobs For the Record Communities For Artists Developers Advertising Investors Vendors Useful links Support Free"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d03", "start": 0, "end": 603, "text": "Crusaders The Cult The Dazz Band The Deirdre Wilson Tabac The Delfonics The Dells The Diddys Featuring Paige Douglas The Dramatics The Drifters The Dutch Rhythm Steel & S B The Dynamic Superiors The Dynamics The Earth Disciples The Ebonys The Eight Minutes The Eleventh Hour The Elgins The Eliminators The Emotions ‎ The Entertainers The Esquires The Essential Northern Soul Story The Everyday People The Exciters The Fabulous Counts The Facts Of Life The Family Circle The Fantastics ‎ The Fatback Band The fifth Dimension The Five Stairsteps The Floaters The Four Mints The Four Tops The Free Movement"}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d03", "start": 605, "end": 737, "text": "The album \"Golden Hits\" features a collection of classic tracks by The Fatback Band, showcasing their unique blend of funk and soul."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d03", "start": 738, "end": 843, "text": "This compilation highlights some of their most beloved hits, making it a must-have for fans of the genre."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d04", "start": 0, "end": 21, "text": "The Magic of Boney M."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d04", "start": 22, "end": 60, "text": "– 20 Golden Hits The Magic of Boney M."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d04", "start": 61, "end": 135, "text": "– 20 Golden Hits is a greatest hits album by Euro-Caribbean group Boney M."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d04", "start": 136, "end": 290, "text": "issued in February 1980 which contained all their biggest hits up until that point, including non-album singles \"Mary's Boy Child/Oh My Lord\" and \"Hooray!"}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d04", "start": 291, "end": 298, "text": "Hooray!"}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d04", "start": 299, "end": 561, "text": "It's A Holi-Holiday\", key album tracks from \"Take The Heat Off Me\", \"Love for Sale\", \"Nightflight to Venus\" and \"Oceans of Fantasy\" as well as their most recent double A-side single release \"I See A Boat On The River\"/ \"My Friend Jack\" (Germany #5 and Norway#6)."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d04", "start": 562, "end": 565, "text": "The"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d05", "start": 0, "end": 119, "text": "The Golden Hits of Sandie Shaw The Golden Hits of Sandie Shaw is a compilation album by the British singer Sandie Shaw."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d05", "start": 120, "end": 414, "text": "Released in April 1966 by Pye Records on their budget Golden Guinea label, it contains all of the \"A\" sides and \"B\" sides of all her UK chart singles from 1964 to the end of 1965, which was technically all of her singles apart from her first which had failed to make an impression on the chart."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d05", "start": 415, "end": 479, "text": "The \"Golden Hits\" compilation did not enter the UK Albums Chart."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d05", "start": 480, "end": 521, "text": "This album has never been released on CD."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d05", "start": 522, "end": 528, "text": "Of the"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d06", "start": 0, "end": 483, "text": "of Sandie Shaw '' – news · newspapers · books · scholar · JSTOR ( November 2018 ) 1966 greatest hits album by Sandie Shaw The Golden Hits of Sandie Shaw Greatest hits album by Sandie Shaw Released 1966 Genre Pop Label Pye Sandie Shaw chronology Me ( 1965 ) The Golden Hits of Sandie Shaw ( 1966 ) Puppet on a String ( 1967 ) Professional ratings Review scores Source Rating Record Mirror [ 1 ] The Golden Hits of Sandie Shaw is a compilation album by the British singer Sandie Shaw ."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d06", "start": 484, "end": 513, "text": "Released in April 1966 by Pye"}, "D8S1": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d07", "start": 0, "end": 537, "text": "4 November 2024 0 Tuesday 5 November 2024 0 Wednesday 6 November 2024 0 Thursday 7 November 2024 0 Friday 8 November 2024 0 Saturday 9 November 2024 0 Sunday 10 November 2024 0 Monday 11 November 2024 0 Tuesday 12 November 2024 0 Wednesday 13 November 2024 0 Thursday 14 November 2024 0 Friday 15 November 2024 0 Saturday 16 November 2024 0 Sunday 17 November 2024 0 Monday 18 November 2024 0 Tuesday 19 November 2024 0 Wednesday 20 November 2024 0 Thursday 21 November 2024 0 Friday 22 November 2024 0 Saturday 23 November 2024 0 Sunday"}, "D9S1": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0359-d81ec72d0be8:d08", "start": 0, "end": 580, "text": "ClassicRockHistory.com Inter